<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jair Bolsonaro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1955">1955</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jair Bolsonaro is a Brazilian right-wing politician and former army captain who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> from 2019 to 2022. His presidency was marked by conflict with the courts and the press, rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deforestation">deforestation</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> and a contested response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/covid-19-pandemic">COVID-19 pandemic</a>. After he lost the 2022 election to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva">Lula</a>, his supporters stormed government buildings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasilia">Brasília</a>, and in 2025 the Supreme Court convicted him of plotting a coup.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jair-bolsonaro.jpg" alt="Jair Bolsonaro" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isac Nóbrega/PR · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jair_Bolsonaro_em_24_de_abril_de_2019_(1)_(3x4).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
